# MindEd Connections — Coding Standards

> The full standards document is `STANDARDS.md` at the repo root. This file is the enforced summary for Cursor.

---

## Frontend (Next.js)

- Named exports only — default exports only in `page.tsx` files.
- `"use client"` only when state, effects, or browser APIs are needed. Keep client components small.
- Tailwind first for all styling. Use CSS design tokens (`var(--sage-500)`, `var(--linen)`, `var(--ink)`, etc.) — never raw hex values or hard-coded px sizes.
- All imports use the `@/` alias. Import order: React/Next → third-party → components → lib → types.
- `import * as React from "react"` — never the default import.
- No form libraries — native `<form>` with local state validation before submission.
- Every interactive element needs keyboard access, a visible focus ring, and ARIA labels where required. Target WCAG 2.1 AA.
- Use `next/image` for all images, `next/link` for all internal navigation.
- Do not add `"use client"` to layouts or pages when only a child needs it.

## Backend (ASP.NET Core)

- **Fat service / thin controller.** Controllers are HTTP translation only (≤ 15 lines per action). All business logic, EF queries, and Identity calls live in services under `Services/<Domain>/`.
- Services throw typed domain exceptions (`ValidationException`, `NotFoundException`, `ConflictException`, `UnauthorizedException`). Controllers catch these and map to HTTP status codes — nothing else.
- Every list endpoint is paginated. Use `PaginatedQuery` (base) and `PagedResponse<T>` from `MindedConnections.Shared`.
- Structured Serilog logging at the service layer only. Use message templates — never string interpolation: `_logger.LogInformation("Created {UserId}", id)` not `$"Created {id}"`.
- Rate limiting on all public and auth endpoints using ASP.NET Core's built-in `RateLimiter` middleware.
- All EF calls must be async (`ToListAsync`, `FirstOrDefaultAsync`, `SaveChangesAsync`). Never `ToList()` before `Where()`. Use `Select()` projections — never return full entity graphs to the API layer.
- Secrets (`Jwt:Secret`, connection strings) go in `appsettings.Development.json` (gitignored) or environment variables — never committed to source control.

## Documentation

- Every directory with source code must have a `README.md`. Create one before adding code to an undocumented directory.
- READMEs must cover: purpose, what belongs here, file list with one-line descriptions, conventions specific to this directory.
- Update the README whenever you change the directory's contents or structure.
- Do not copy `STANDARDS.md` content into READMEs — link to the relevant section number instead.
- TypeScript: JSDoc (`/** */`) on exported functions and hooks where the name alone doesn't explain the purpose.
- C#: XML doc comments (`///`) on all public service interface members.

## Universal rules

- No business logic in controllers
- No raw hex colors or hard-coded pixel values (frontend)
- No `async void` — always `async Task`
- No `.Result` / `.Wait()` on async calls
- No unbounded list endpoints
- No logging of passwords, tokens, or PII
- No `export default` outside of Next.js page files
- No commented-out code — delete it, git has history
- No dead imports
